        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in openssl. When a server replaces its security context during an active Transport Layer Security (TLS) handshake, it fails to update the internal capacity tracking for cryptographic signature algorithms. A remote peer can exploit this issue by advertising specific signature algorithms, causing out-of-bounds memory reads and writes on the server heap. This vulnerability can corrupt internal memory and terminate the process, resulting in a Denial of Service (DoS).",
