          {
            "category": "workaround",
            "details": "Do not revoke certificates over CMP by supplying a PKCS#10 CSR (`openssl cmp -cmd rr -csr ...` or `OSSL_CMP_CTX_set1_p10CSR()`). Identify the certificate by certificate or by issuer name and serial number instead. Restrict CMP clients to trusted CMP servers and protect CMP message-protection credentials ([CME-203](https://cmetaxonomy.org/entries/CME-203.html)). If CMP certificate revocation is unused, avoid enabling CMP client revocation workflows.",
            "product_ids": [
              "Red Hat Hardened Images:openssl3-0:3.5.9-0.1.hum1@src",
