            "text": "A flaw was found in OpenSSL. A remote attacker can cause a Denial of Service (DoS) by flooding a connection with connection identifier update requests while withholding acknowledgments. This behavior bypasses connection limits and forces the system to accumulate pending retirement frames, resulting in excessive memory consumption.",
